            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0457" n="363" xml:id="pg363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00/852: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-17T19:00:00-05:00">October 17, 1930—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>89. Your 144, October 16, noon. If the British Chargé in Liberia deems it
                    advisable to request a British warship, and if the British Government decides to
                    send such a vessel, I do not perceive any objection to this course. You may
                    inform your British colleague accordingly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
